{
  "_about": "Shared internal-HTTP flow cases: one stream opened by a RequestHead declaring body_len, then frames from the caller (client) or the serving app (server), each with the verdict every flow keeper must give it: ok, or fault (refused, ending the stream). Written by hand. Read by the kernel's StreamFlow (kernel::apps::ihttp_flow_corpus_tests) and the page's IhttpRouter (host/__tests__/ihttp-flow-corpus.test.ts). A case stops at its first fault or Cancel. A second RequestHead is not a flow step: the relay and the page both treat it as a replay (E8), outside StreamFlow. Cases the two keep differently today (a Cancel after the caller's own End, credit sent before the response head, a body shorter than declared at End) join when W2 makes them agree.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a_bodyless_get_and_its_answer",
      "body_len": 0,
      "steps": [
        {
          "from": "client",
          "kind": "End",
          "expect": "ok"
        },
        {
          "from": "server",
          "kind": "ResponseHead",
          "body_len": null,
          "expect": "ok"
        },
        {
          "from": "server",
          "kind": "Body",
          "len": 3,
          "expect": "ok"
        },
        {
          "from": "server",
          "kind": "End",
          "expect": "ok"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a_request_body_exactly_its_declared_length",
      "body_len": 8,
      "steps": [
        {
          "from": "client",
          "kind": "Body",
          "len": 4,
          "expect": "ok"
        },
        {
          "from": "client",
          "kind": "Body",
          "len": 4,
          "expect": "ok"
        },
        {
          "from": "client",
          "kind": "End",
          "expect": "ok"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a_request_body_longer_than_declared",
